## Changes Implemented

### 1. Fix 1 (`s4wp3-report-verifier-retypes-unopenable`)
- **Root Cause**: [`verify_migration_report`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L560-L666) was catching bare `Exception` around opening and probing the target arrival ledger and re-typing any failure as [`ReportHeadMismatchRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L297-L299), asserting that the head differs when the store could not be opened or read (e.g. `StoreLost` from `ArrivalTornTail`).
- **Fix**:
  - Introduced [`ReportTargetUnopenableRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L302-L314) (subclass of [`ReportVerificationRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L281-L283)) carrying `target_path` and `cause`.
  - Replaced the bare `except Exception` with a typed catch: `except (StoreLost, ArrivalTornTail, ArrivalCorrupt, GenesisRefused, OSError) as exc: raise ReportTargetUnopenableRefused(...) from exc`.
  - [`ReportHeadMismatchRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L297-L299) is now raised exclusively after a successful ledger open and head read when the claimed head tuple does not match the live head.
  - Exported [`ReportTargetUnopenableRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/__init__.py#L49-L100) from [`migrate`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/__init__.py) and [`migrate.refusals`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py).
  - Added test in [`test_verify_migration_report_causes`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/tests/test_sidecar.py#L946-L962) against a torn-tail target verifying `ReportTargetUnopenableRefused` is raised and carries `StoreLost` / `ArrivalTornTail` in the cause chain rather than `ReportHeadMismatchRefused`.

### 2. Fix 2 (`s4wp3-migrate-undeclared-ckdl-bypasses-lang`)
- **Fix**:
  - Added `"ckdl>=1.0"` matching `libs/lang/pyproject.toml` to dependencies in [`libs/migrate/pyproject.toml`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/pyproject.toml#L8-L14).
  - Added required loud comment at the direct import site in [`libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L76-L77):
